Subject: [PATCH] fall back to pure-PyTorch deformable attention on newer GPUs

mmcv-full's compiled `_ext` ships SASS for sm_50..sm_86 and embeds no PTX, so
there is no JIT path onto newer cards. On anything above sm_86 -- Blackwell
here -- the compiled multi-scale deformable attention kernel launches with
"CUDA error: no kernel image is available for execution on the device".

Upstream gates on `torch.cuda.is_available() and value.is_cuda`, which is true
on exactly the cards where the kernel does not work. Gate on compute capability
instead and fall back to `multi_scale_deformable_attn_pytorch`, which is
numerically equivalent and device-agnostic, just slower.

Override with DRIVE_JEPA_MSDA=compiled|pytorch.

